.TH JTUTIL-MP4 1 "August 2026" "JTFRAME" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jtutil-mp4 \- create an MP4 video from simulation frames and audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jtutil mp4
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates an MP4 video from PNG frames and the accompanying \fBtest.wav\fR.
By default, it reads \fBframes/frame_*.png\fR and \fBtest.wav\fR below the
current directory. The \fB-p\fR option selects another simulation directory.
.PP
Frames are copied into a temporary directory below \fB/tmp\fR. Missing frame
numbers are filled by copying the preceding available frame, without changing
the source frames. Both \fBframe_*.png\fR and \fBframes_*.png\fR names are
accepted.
.PP
The default frame rate is read from \fBJTFRAME_RATE\fR in the current core's
\fBcfg/macros.def\fR when available. Otherwise, it is 60 Hz. Simulation
scripts pass their measured frame rate explicitly.
.PP
The default output name is \fBtest.mp4\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-p, --path " directory
Simulation directory containing \fBtest.wav\fR and \fBframes/\fR.
.TP
.BI "-o, --output " file
Output MP4 file. The default is \fBtest.mp4\fR.
.TP
.BI "-r, --rate " hz
Override the video frame rate in Hz.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
